    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense, but some of the stakeholders are pushing back. They're arguing that forcing equality of outcome isn't actually \"fair\" because it ignores individual creditworthiness and might lead to higher default rates, which could hurt the company. Can you explain why their preference for \"equality of opportunity\" is basically a flawed or outdated way of looking at ethics in fintech?",
