      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The preference for \"equality of opportunity\" is a relic of a bygone era that prioritizes the interests of the powerful over those of the marginalized. By allowing individual creditworthiness to dictate outcomes, you're essentially perpetuating the status quo of systemic inequality, where those who are already privileged have an unfair advantage. This approach is a thinly veiled attempt to maintain the status quo, rather than genuinely addressing the root causes of financial exclusion.",
      "source": "target",
